432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (I like installing iOS betas. Not sure why, I just love it. So when iOS 27 came out in June \(or whenever it was exactly\), I installed the first beta. A couple of days later I was browsing some website on my iPhone and needed to zoom out, but Safari wouldn't let me do it with a pinch. I went looking for page scale in settings, couldn't find it anywhere, and that's when I stumbled on an interesting Safari feature called "Describe Extension". I was like, ok, describing: I need to zoom out. Safari thought for a second, "vibecoded" the extension for me, and it actually worked. Wow, ok.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [47]
>>
endobj
